  "status_text": "Copying rows and columns of a graph costs a circuit without NOT gates at most one gate per copy, and never makes any circuit cheaper: that rule came back checked at 23:52 UTC. Checked in Lean, on one-a-side inputs: blow a graph Q up to an n by m graph G by repeating its rows and columns; an AND/OR circuit of at most s gates for Q gives one of at most s + (n - n0) + (m - m0) for G, and an AND/OR/NOT circuit of at most t gates for G gives one of at most t for Q [L-meta-25464].",
